  "worked_solution": "The area $A$ can be approximated using the formula\n\n$$\nA≈(\\overset{\\text{heights}}{\\overset{⏞}{f(20)+f(30)+f(40)}})\\cdot {{Δt}_{⏟}}_{\\text{width}}.\n$$\n\nSo, we now set up a table with the values of $f(t)$ at each point:\n\n| $t$ | $20$ | $30$ | $40$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(t)$ | $12$ | $k$ | $16$ |\n\nSo, we obtain the following approximation to the area:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ≈(12+k+16)\\cdot 10 \\\\  & =(28+k)\\cdot 10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we are given that $A$ must be $480$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(28+k)\\cdot 10 & =480 \\\\ 28+k & =48 \\\\ k & =20.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
